## Project structure

```
config/
  languages.json
  seo.json

src/
  app/
    components/
    services/
    views/
    routes.ts
    main.ts
  assets/
  core/   -- Nutin framework source
  styles/

tools/    -- build, development, generator and testing

nutin.config.js
```

## Running your app

```bash
# Development
{{packageManager}} run serve # build and serve
{{packageManager}} run dev   # build and serve with live reload

# Build
{{packageManager}} run build      # build the application
{{packageManager}} run build:prod # build the application for production
```

## Imports

Imports must use **relative paths** and end with `.js` extension.

```js
import { MyModule } from 'relative/path/to/my-module.js';
```

## Generate components, views and services

Generated elements are automatically exported from the corresponding barrel file:
`src/app/<components|views|services>/index.ts`.


```bash
{{packageManager}} run generate <component|view|service> ELEMENT_NAME

# Examples
{{packageManager}} run generate component my-component # Target dir: src/app/components/my-component/
{{packageManager}} run generate component path/to/my-component/ # Target dir: src/app/components/path/to/my-component/
```

## A typical component

```bash
components/
  product-card/
    product-card.component.html
    product-card.component.scss
    product-card.component.ts
```

```ts
// The builder replaces __TEMPLATE_PLACEHOLDER__ with the component's .html template.
const templateFn = (product: Product) => `__TEMPLATE_PLACEHOLDER__`;

export class ProductCardComponent extends Component {
  private _product: Product;

  constructor(mountTarget: HTMLElement, config: Product) {
    super({ templateFn, mountTarget, config });
    this._product = config;
  }

  // Declares children mounted into the data-component / data-catalog placeholders below.
  public childConfigs(): ComponentConfig[] {
    // Single child, matched to <div data-component="product-details">
    const detailsComponent = {
      selector: `product-details`,
      factory: (el) => new ProductDetailsComponent(
        el,
        this._product.details,
      )
    };

    // One child per item in _product.tags, matched to <div data-catalog="product-tags">
    const tagsCatalog = this.catalogConfig({
      selector: 'product-tags',
      array: this._product.tags,
      component: ProductTagsComponent,
      elementName: 'product-tag'
    });

    return [
      detailsComponent,
      ...tagsCatalog
    ];
  }

  private _goToProductPage(productId: string): void {
    Navigation.navigateTo(`/product/${productId}`);
  }
}
```

```html
<div
  data-event="click:_goToProductPage:${product.id}"
  class="product-card"
>
  <h2 class="product-card__name">${product.name}</h2>
  <div data-component="product-details"></div>
  <div data-catalog="product-tags"></div>
</div>
```

```scss
.product-card {
  // component styles
}

.product-card__name {
  // element styles
}
```

## Features and configuration

Nutin features are enabled in `nutin.config.js`.

### `nutin.config.js`

Main Nutin configuration and tool options. See the inline comments for details.

- `tailwind`, `i18n`, `inlineTemplates`, `generateSEOFiles` — top-level features.
- `generator.*` — controls what the generator scaffolds.
- `builder.*` — controls build behavior.
- `testinNutin.*` — controls TestinNutin.

### `config/seo.json`

- Register your routes' description, title and ogImage here.
- Data is used to generate static `index.html` per route, `robots.txt`, and `sitemap.xml`.
- Unused if `nutin.config.js -> generateSEOFiles` is disabled.

### `config/languages.json`

- Register supported languages for i18n here.
- Unused if `nutin.config.js -> i18n` is disabled.

## Styling

- Nutin uses SASS (`.scss` syntax, compatible with plain CSS) as its default styling solution.

- Tailwind CSS v4 is also supported as an optional utility-first CSS layer.

**IMPORTANT:** Installing Tailwind CSS dependencies will print warnings `npm warn install-scripts`.

This is expected (npm 12's default install-script allowlisting) and safe to ignore.
If you want the warning gone anyway, run `npm install-scripts approve <package>`, but note this grants that package's install scripts blanket trust on every future install.

## Global layout components

If you need components to render outside `<main>` (such as `<header>` or `<footer>`), initialize them in `main.ts`. 

Those components are outside the `View`s rendering target (`<main id="app">`), so they will be present on each route.

*Note*: `View` subclasses inherit `hideHeader()` / `revealHeader()` and `hideFooter()` / `revealFooter()`, which target the elements with the corresponding id (`#header` and `#footer`).

```ts
class App {
  private _header: HeaderComponent;
  private _footer: FooterComponent;
  private _mountTarget = 'body' as unknown as HTMLElement;

  constructor() {
    registerPipes();
    AppRouter(appRoutes);

    this._header = new HeaderComponent(this._mountTarget);
    document.body.prepend(this.header.render());

    this._footer = new FooterComponent(this._mountTarget);
    document.body.append(this.footer.render());
  }
}
```

## Testing

You can use any testing tool you prefer for application code.

This project includes TestinNutin, Nutin's lightweight testing toolkit. Nutin itself is tested exclusively with it, and the tests are included in the generated project so you can:
- use them as executable documentation;
- run and modify Nutin's tests when modifying its code.

Run the tests with:

`{{packageManager}} run testin-nutin`

To use TestinNutin for application tests, enable:

```js
// nutin.config.js
testinNutin: {
  includeApp: true,
}
```
*Note:* TestinNutin files use root imports.
```js
import { MyModule } from '#root/dist/src/path/to/my-module.js';
```

See [TestinNutin docs](https://nutin.org/docs/testin-nutin).

